{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Markdown provides HTML, React, and Octane renderers over the same AST."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n\nconst html = renderHtml(source)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"import { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nconst article = <Markdown>{source}</Markdown>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"import { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/octane'\n\n<Markdown>{source}</Markdown>","lang":"tsrx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"core-parity","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core parity"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core syntax is tested so server-rendered React and Octane markup and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderHtml"},{"type":"text","value":" have equivalent structure. Serializer differences such as boolean attributes, trailing style semicolons, and whitespace between block elements are normalized in parity tests."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer-specific boundaries are excluded from this guarantee:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React and Octane "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"components"},{"type":"text","value":" replacements"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extension "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderHtml"},{"type":"text","value":" hooks"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"trusted raw HTML injection"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"highlighter output"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"lists","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lists"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tight lists render paragraph content directly under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<li>"},{"type":"text","value":". Loose lists preserve "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<p>"},{"type":"text","value":" wrappers. Task-list checkboxes stay inline with their labels in either form. A loose nested list does not make its parent list loose, and ordered lists preserve a starting value of zero."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"code-blocks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code blocks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Without a highlighter, code is escaped and rendered as a small "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<pre><code>"},{"type":"text","value":" tree. A titled fence adds a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<figure>"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<figcaption>"},{"type":"text","value":". The renderer records language, filename, framework, and line metadata as classes and data attributes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"highlighter"},{"type":"text","value":" callback, the returned HTML becomes the contents of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<code>"},{"type":"text","value":". The callback is a trusted boundary."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"heading-anchors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Heading anchors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Heading IDs are a parse concern. Visible anchor links are a render concern and are disabled by default:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"renderHtml(document, {\n  headingAnchors: {\n    content: '#',\n    className: 'heading-anchor',\n    ariaHidden: true,\n    tabIndex: -1,\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rendering-individual-nodes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering individual nodes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderBlock"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderInline"},{"type":"text","value":" render one AST node. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderDocument"},{"type":"text","value":" is the document-specific alias of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderHtml"},{"type":"text","value":". React exposes corresponding "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderBlockReact"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderInlineReact"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderMarkdownReact"},{"type":"text","value":" functions."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"rendering","text":"Rendering","level":1},{"id":"core-parity","text":"Core parity","level":2},{"id":"lists","text":"Lists","level":2},{"id":"code-blocks","text":"Code blocks","level":2},{"id":"heading-anchors","text":"Heading anchors","level":2},{"id":"rendering-individual-nodes","text":"Rendering individual nodes","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Rendering\n\nTanStack Markdown provides HTML, React, and Octane renderers over the same AST.\n\n```ts\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n\nconst html = renderHtml(source)\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nconst article = <Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n```\n\n```tsrx\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/octane'\n\n<Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n```\n\n## Core parity\n\nCore syntax is tested so server-rendered React and Octane markup and `renderHtml` have equivalent structure. Serializer differences such as boolean attributes, trailing style semicolons, and whitespace between block elements are normalized in parity tests.\n\nRenderer-specific boundaries are excluded from this guarantee:\n\n- React and Octane `components` replacements\n- extension `renderHtml` hooks\n- trusted raw HTML injection\n- highlighter output\n\n## Lists\n\nTight lists render paragraph content directly under `<li>`. Loose lists preserve `<p>` wrappers. Task-list checkboxes stay inline with their labels in either form. A loose nested list does not make its parent list loose, and ordered lists preserve a starting value of zero.\n\n## Code blocks\n\nWithout a highlighter, code is escaped and rendered as a small `<pre><code>` tree. A titled fence adds a `<figure>` and `<figcaption>`. The renderer records language, filename, framework, and line metadata as classes and data attributes.\n\nWith a `highlighter` callback, the returned HTML becomes the contents of `<code>`. The callback is a trusted boundary.\n\n## Heading anchors\n\nHeading IDs are a parse concern. Visible anchor links are a render concern and are disabled by default:\n\n```ts\nrenderHtml(document, {\n  headingAnchors: {\n    content: '#',\n    className: 'heading-anchor',\n    ariaHidden: true,\n    tabIndex: -1,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Rendering individual nodes\n\n`renderBlock` and `renderInline` render one AST node. `renderDocument` is the document-specific alias of `renderHtml`. React exposes corresponding `renderBlockReact`, `renderInlineReact`, and `renderMarkdownReact` functions.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Rendering\n---\n\n# Rendering\n\nTanStack Markdown provides HTML, React, and Octane renderers over the same AST.\n\n```ts\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\n\nconst html = renderHtml(source)\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nconst article = <Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n```\n\n```tsrx\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/octane'\n\n<Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n```\n\n## Core parity\n\nCore syntax is tested so server-rendered React and Octane markup and `renderHtml` have equivalent structure. Serializer differences such as boolean attributes, trailing style semicolons, and whitespace between block elements are normalized in parity tests.\n\nRenderer-specific boundaries are excluded from this guarantee:\n\n- React and Octane `components` replacements\n- extension `renderHtml` hooks\n- trusted raw HTML injection\n- highlighter output\n\n## Lists\n\nTight lists render paragraph content directly under `<li>`. Loose lists preserve `<p>` wrappers. Task-list checkboxes stay inline with their labels in either form. A loose nested list does not make its parent list loose, and ordered lists preserve a starting value of zero.\n\n## Code blocks\n\nWithout a highlighter, code is escaped and rendered as a small `<pre><code>` tree. A titled fence adds a `<figure>` and `<figcaption>`. The renderer records language, filename, framework, and line metadata as classes and data attributes.\n\nWith a `highlighter` callback, the returned HTML becomes the contents of `<code>`. The callback is a trusted boundary.\n\n## Heading anchors\n\nHeading IDs are a parse concern. Visible anchor links are a render concern and are disabled by default:\n\n```ts\nrenderHtml(document, {\n  headingAnchors: {\n    content: '#',\n    className: 'heading-anchor',\n    ariaHidden: true,\n    tabIndex: -1,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Rendering individual nodes\n\n`renderBlock` and `renderInline` render one AST node. `renderDocument` is the document-specific alias of `renderHtml`. React exposes corresponding `renderBlockReact`, `renderInlineReact`, and `renderMarkdownReact` functions.\n"}
